WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.640
Present Day

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.590
Present Time

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:23.340
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:28.540
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:33.290
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.560
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.960
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.430
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:49.190
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:54.850
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.970
I have lost it all

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:26.990
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.630
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.840
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.380
I am losing

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.580
Help me to breathe

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:14.190
If people can connect to one another, even the smallest voice will grow loud.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:18.690
If people can connect to one another, even their lives will become longer.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.100
So...

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.820
Lain? I'm coming in.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.150
Lain?

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.670
Thanks.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:04.240
But I already verified that register a long time ago.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.760
That's hilarious!

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.510
Right...

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:17.120
I can't wait for the next-gen protocol to come out.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.390
When it does, I could...

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:26.280
Why are you guys so nice to me?

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.900
No, that's not what I think.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.510
It's just a little strange.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:38.140
I don't have many friends.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:45.300
Thanks, Knights.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.930
Yeah, right!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.580
Hard at work studying, I see...

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.430
Listen, Lain...

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.020
It's like you're going back to your old self lately.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.700
Come hang out with us again sometime.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:13.570
Life's depressing when you're alone all the time!

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.040
I know, but I'm not alone.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.180
Huh? Who's with you, then?

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.680
Everybody comes to see me.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.820
No, that's not right...

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.290
Maybe I go to see them.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.150
What? The Wired, you mean?

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:33.380
A net-pal isn't the same as a real friend.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:36.600
Reika sure is an old fogey when it comes to some things, huh?

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.190
Yeah, an old fogey!

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.450
So what if I am?

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.830
Anyway, Lain, what kind of sites have you been hanging out at?

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:49.340
It's a secret.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.580
Oh, acting high and mighty, huh?

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:54.480
Come on, tell us!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.020
Hey, this'll look good!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.620
No way! You should just give up!

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.590
I think this one's better.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:05.180
No way! This one's better! Right, Lain?

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:09.330
Hey, let's go to that store we went to the other day.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.860
They say they're having a 30-minute all-you-can-eat ice cream special today.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:13.860
I'm hungry!

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.410
Huh?

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:33.510
What? What is it?

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.320
What's with that kid?

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.020
Beats me.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.700
Come on, let's go!

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.170
Let's go, Lain.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.650
Lain, what's...

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:37.920
No way!

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.590
What is that?

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.950
What the?

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.090
Lain? That's...

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.730
You've certainly been coming home early lately.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:32.750
Now it's Lain who's staying out late.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.680
Do you think you'll get that college recommendation?

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.270
Speak of the devil.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.900
A strange phenomenon appeared in the skies above Tokyo today.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:06.440
People in the area who observed it report being deeply unnerved by it.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.440
Was this a malicious prank?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.610
Was it merely a natural phenomenon, or was it a deliberate act?

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.050
Hello, Navi.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.780
Hello, Lain.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.220
Connect to Wired.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:40.070
So you're Lain, huh?

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:47.650
You're somethin' else, to be able to translate your real world form

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:50.120
so well here into the Wired.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.120
Stupid Cheshire Cat wannabe...

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:59.160
"Wannabe," nothing. At my user level, this is the best I can do.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:01.930
Most people can only manage ears.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.230
I'm way better than them, don't you think?

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.430
Shut your hole. Just give me the information.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:13.470
I helped Lain. This is gonna make me a hero with the local users.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.670
You're more noise than signal.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:19.180
Tell me about the game that all the grade-schoolers are playing.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:22.820
A game? There's all kinds of kids' games.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.480
Moron.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:27.550
You've got a hunch that tells you it's a game?

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.890
To a kid, anything can be a game.

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.750
So you called up the search result...

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:40.540
Now I get it. This man might know the answer.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.670
The child-killer scientist.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:56.480
You live up to your reputation, Lain! You searched him on your own!

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:01.480
In the real world, he's just an old man waiting to die in a private hospital ward.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:08.520
I helped you.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.760
A little.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:17.130
Ask him about KIDS.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:23.730
I already know. You're not much of a guide, Cheshire Cat.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:30.140
Now it's your turn, Professor Hodgeson.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:32.420
Tell me all about it.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:14.960
You look very lifelike, young lady.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.520
What's "KIDS"?

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.400
It's so peaceful here...

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:30.170
I want to relax here until my body rots in the real world.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.510
You know what's happening, don't you?

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.580
What's "KIDS"?

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:42.540
Time passes so beautifully here. And quietly, as if it will last forever.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:47.550
Show me the experiment data from 15 years ago, Professor Hodgeson.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:53.590
I never meant to put the children in any danger.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:59.350
I don't mean 15 years ago, I mean the game that all the kids are playing now.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:03.370
They're reproducing your experiment, aren't they?

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:07.580
Somebody dug it out of the trash can.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:11.860
I thought I had erased all the data.

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:16.080
Tell me about the Kensington Experiment.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:27.030
Psi, parapsychological ability, is present in most children,

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:30.130
although very faint in most.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:37.110
It's nothing as outrageous as ESP.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:43.310
It's just good intuition, or enough physical ability to bend a coin.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:46.620
What're these that are attached to their heads?

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:51.070
We called them Outer Receptors.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:53.950
That's what receives the Psi.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:58.660
This is KIDS.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:02.740
Individually, their Psi may be weak,

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:04.900
but if I could collect their power...

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.110
What were you expecting?

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:09.280
Something beyond imagining.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:11.840
That's what I wanted to see, young lady.

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:16.090
What did you make them do?

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:20.310
Science isn't merely about proving hypotheses.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.610
That's what I believed.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:24.690
That's not what I mean!

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:30.110
So, you didn't give any thought to the children.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.300
As you say.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.770
It was the KID System that converted the weak

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:38.000
electromagentic waves of the brain received by the Outer Receptors

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:42.080
and enhanced the functions of a specific area of the brain.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:46.740
That is what KIDS really is.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:01.350
When the children's Psi was combined, how much energy was generated?

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:06.830
Stop it...

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.480
Enough!

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:16.820
I smashed KIDS to pieces so that it could never be rebuilt.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:26.880
But its schematics found their way onto the Wired

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:30.040
and eventually coalesced somewhere.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:34.050
Someone found them,

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:38.670
and updated it so that it could manifest

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:43.160
phenomena without Outer Receptors.

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:48.670
If it can influence these new children to that extent as an emulation,

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.780
I'm forced to acknowledge their talent.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.650
Is that all you can think about?

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.610
You don't care about the children?

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.720
No matter how much I punish myself,

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:04.120
those children won't return to the real world.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.820
And there's even less that I can do about this current group.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.560
Talk about self-centered.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:15.340
So who's using it now?

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:16.800
Young lady...

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:22.510
All this talking has worn me out.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:24.180
It was nice meeting you.

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:28.350
I don't know what you plan to do in the Wired

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:31.750
or what sort of being you're trying to become,

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:36.120
but you're powerful. Incredibly powerful.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:42.380
If there really is a god here in the Wired, you're a blessed child.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:46.030
I... I'm not...

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:51.330
I wonder where the power of the rogues that run the KIDS emulation

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:55.210
and this other kind of power come from?

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.740
Rogues?

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:02.720
If you'll excuse me then,

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:05.050
I'm a little tired.

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:09.520
My body's time has run out.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:15.480
My wish has come true.

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:41.520
Knights...

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.590
Shut up!

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:05.910
Who are you people? Why did you try to tell me all this?

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:14.180
Was I just your toy? Is this all a game?

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:17.480
What do you want to use the children for?

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:19.420
Are you just doing it for kicks?

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:26.360
You'll do anything if you can do it and if you think it'll be fun!

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.770
Then you're just a bunch of losers!

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:43.070
Aren't you going to speak up? Isn't anybody going to answer?

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:30.650
Them!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.990
Now I get it!

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:50.640
You!

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:54.610
You're Knights, right?

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:02.230
You are, aren't you? You're Knights, right?

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:07.320
Please get down.

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:13.470
W-What the hell was that?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:18.250
The coolant system in your room.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:25.710
They must've planted a parasite bomb in your coolant system.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:28.420
It almost sounds like you're saying you didn't do it.

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:32.760
It wasn't us.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.420
Who was it, then?

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.360
Who did it?!

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:48.200
The Knights.

00:22:29.150 --> 00:22:33.580
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:29.150 --> 00:22:33.580
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:37.490
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:37.490
now I am punished.

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:43.790
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:43.790
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:44.510 --> 00:22:50.700
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:44.510 --> 00:22:50.700
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:57.250 --> 00:23:01.890
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:57.250 --> 00:23:01.890
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:01.890 --> 00:23:06.340
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:01.890 --> 00:23:06.340
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:12.530
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:12.530
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:19.770
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:19.770
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:27.820
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:27.820
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:37.730
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:37.730
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:43.340
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:43.340
You probably don't know

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:51.050
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:51.050
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
